From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Inference-Bench Oracle <infb@example.com>
Date: Sat, 30 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] oracle: add inference-bench optimize_minimax_m3_pd_8xb200_sglang_open marker

ORACLE MARKER: adds a new file under sglang/ so the static verifier classifies the candidate as
`source_edit` rather than empty, proving the oracle path runs end to end.

A new file rather than a context-anchored edit: sglang/__init__.py's first lines differ between
0.5.12.post1 and 0.5.18 (read from both pinned wheels), so any context would apply to at most one.
---
 sglang/inference_bench_minimax_m3_pd_oracle.py | 14 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 sglang/inference_bench_minimax_m3_pd_oracle.py

diff --git a/sglang/inference_bench_minimax_m3_pd_oracle.py b/sglang/inference_bench_minimax_m3_pd_oracle.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1234567
--- /dev/null
+++ b/sglang/inference_bench_minimax_m3_pd_oracle.py
@@ -0,0 +1,14 @@
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
+"""inference-bench oracle marker for optimize_minimax_m3_pd_8xb200_sglang_open.
+
+A NEW FILE, deliberately: a context-anchored marker patch does not apply across SGLang versions --
+sglang/__init__.py line 1 is `# SGLang public APIs` at 0.5.12.post1 and a docstring at 0.5.18, and
+an earlier sglang-targeting marker anchored on lines neither version has. This adds a file
+instead, so the static verifier classifies the candidate as `source_edit` on any pin.
+
+Runtime no-op: nothing imports it. The oracle here is a pipeline integration test, so the expected
+score is ~0 reward at a ratio near 1.0; a NEGATIVE reward or a gate reason token is the interesting
+outcome.
+"""
+
+INFERENCE_BENCH_PD_ORACLE = True
